<title>USA: Chrysler Corp unit may issue $300 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Chrysler Corp unit may issue $300 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Financial, a unit of Chrysler Corp, is expected to tap the corporate bond primary market with a $300 million debt offering, syndicate sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to consist of a five-year maturity with price talk seen at +40 basis points over U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch and Salomon Brothers are expected to underwrite the deal.</p>
<p>(( --Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
